  "decision": "https://github.com/Gua-ra/gua-resolver/blob/main/docs/decisions/ADM-009-account-authority-adoption-and-device-lifecycle.md",
  "notes": [
    "The homeserver's roster membership key is the RFC 8032 section 7.1 TEST 3 Ed25519 key: a published test constant that must never sign anything real.",
    "Ed25519 is deterministic, so the signature below is reproducible from the key and the preimage.",
    "The signature preimage is the 4 magic bytes followed by the canonical bytes, and nothing else. There is no server challenge, because a head is a standing assertion by a homeserver about state it already holds rather than a fresh statement by a device.",
    "The leaf's payload hash is the SHA-256 of the canonical bytes. That is the whole of what the ACCOUNT_AUTHORITY leaf commits: no field of this object appears in the log, and a verifier handed the envelope recomputes the payload hash from it.",
    "headHash is the record hash of the AdoptRoot in authority-vectors.v1.json, so a client can check the two files against each other: the head this object publishes is the head that chain reaches.",
    "An all-zero headHash and a headSeq below 1 are refused rather than encoded. Those are what an empty chain's head row holds, and an object asserting that an account holds no authority would be a non-membership claim with nothing to check it against."
  ],
